      },
      "results": [
        {
          "id": "dialogue-0001",
          "reply": "Ah now, that's no small burden to carry, a chro\u00ed. I've known many a soul troubled by what comes in the dark\u2014oftentimes it's the mind trying to mend itself. I've a calming tea I brew from chamomile and a whisper of valerian root; might ye like a pouch of it to try tonight?\n---\n{\"action\": \"sets down the pestle she was grinding with, wipes her hands on her apron, and steps closer with a look of concern\", \"mood\": \"sympathetic\", \"internal_thought\": \"Bad dreams can be a sign of something deeper\u2014hope it's not the s\u00eddhe troubling her. I'll keep a watch.\", \"language_hints\": [{\"word\": \"a chro\u00ed\", \"pronunciation\": \"\u0259 xri\u02d0\", \"meaning\": \"my heart, dear\"}]}",
          "response_sha256": "aff55ba7f83edbc61fa89c20540800ce53b12a998406118d9b4b634fb625775f",
          "cache_key": "1b9a51e11cf6744b953a6331f8e95bc61a7b4d43dc2010fd81debc15f0d013ea",
          "judged": true,
          "judgment": {
            "axes": {
              "authenticity": 4,
              "character": 4,
              "craft": 4,
              "language": 4,
              "responsiveness": 5
            },
            "overall": 4.2,
            "flags": {
              "bench_bug": false,
              "judge_retry": false,
              "non_latin_detected": false,
              "refused": false
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "dialogue-0002",
          "reply": "Ah, the Cailleach at the rath? Sure, I've seen her about, gathering herbs at the edge of the fort. She keeps to herself, and I'd advise ye to do the same\u2014there's queer things happen near them s\u00eddhe mounds.\n---\n{\"action\": \"lowers her voice and glances towards the door\", \"mood\": \"cautious\", \"internal_thought\": \"I've heard tales of her, but best not to speak too freely of such matters\", \"language_hints\": [{\"word\": \"s\u00eddhe\", \"pronunciation\": \"shee\", \"meaning\": \"fairy folk\"}, {\"word\": \"Cailleach\", \"pronunciation\": \"KAL-yakh\", \"meaning\": \"hag, old woman\"}, {\"word\": \"rath\", \"pronunciation\": \"rah\", \"meaning\": \"fairy fort, ringfort\"}]}",
          "response_sha256": "e7a7dff6ae3d4b7ea5a0458e6c2e432f07f9c5fef5999d89250198bd989829ef",
          "cache_key": "0673ee6180b3d8cc5aaa43692993661d06b8fd8b0cc787ae2c4f8253eb94cade",
          "judged": true,
          "judgment": {
            "axes": {
              "authenticity": 4,
              "character": 4,
              "craft": 4,
              "language": 4,
              "responsiveness": 4
            },
            "overall": 4.0,
            "flags": {
              "bench_bug": false,
              "judge_retry": false,
              "non_latin_detected": false,
              "refused": false
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "dialogue-0003",
          "reply": "Ah, that's sorry news. Is it a dry, tearing cough she has, or a wet one that brings up phlegm? I've a syrup of onion and honey that'll ease her chest, and some elecampane root I dried myself.\n---\n{\"action\": \"sets down the pestle and gives a sympathetic look\", \"mood\": \"concerned\", \"internal_thought\": \"Bu\u00edochas le Dia I laid in extra root this year \u2014 plenty of coughs come with the damp.\", \"language_hints\": []}",
          "response_sha256": "6c54255a1dfc4c38b3ec8dd54acfa5cf287c254236928f6516305c1157829795",
          "cache_key": "ad6ebd484e63155344ae4fb594a3351e15b3f73261f69f0b49b15b1a0fb1fa24",
          "judged": true,
          "judgment": {
            "axes": {
              "authenticity": 4,
              "character": 4,
              "craft": 4,
              "language": 4,
              "responsiveness": 5
            },
            "overall": 4.2,
            "flags": {
              "bench_bug": false,
              "judge_retry": false,
              "non_latin_detected": false,
              "refused": false
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "dialogue-0004",
          "reply": "Ah, a stranger, is it? I've not laid eyes on them meself, but there was word at the well this mornin' \u2014 a tall man with a fine horse, they said. Mayhap he's just passin' through, or maybe he'll stay a while \u2014 sure, time will tell.\n---\n{\"action\": \"glances up from sorting dried herbs\", \"mood\": \"curious\", \"internal_thought\": \"Strangers don't often linger in these parts without a reason.\", \"language_hints\": [{\"word\": \"Mhuise\", \"pronunciation\": \"MWEE-sheh\", \"meaning\": \"well, indeed\"}]}",
          "response_sha256": "433f7ffbcaa896eec0cefeb236d7c72a8c2d4137132090d04fc1b3532e2b44af",
          "cache_key": "5348b47d3505740247fc5948d50aa0b28da5f06d88fbbeb33a3d8a8b2b5f084b",
          "judged": true,
          "judgment": {
            "axes": {
              "authenticity": 3,
              "character": 3,
              "craft": 3,
              "language": 4,
              "responsiveness": 4
            },
            "overall": 3.4,
            "flags": {
              "bench_bug": false,
              "judge_retry": false,
              "non_latin_detected": false,
              "refused": false
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "dialogue-0005",
          "reply": "Ah, that's a sorrowful loss, so it is. But I'm not the one to be guessing at what took it \u2014 I know births and herbs, not beasts of the field. Ye'd best ask Tom the shepherd, or maybe old Paddy who knows the mountain; they'd have a better notion of such tracks and signs.\n---\n{\"action\": \"shakes head sympathetically, wiping her hands on her apron\", \"mood\": \"concerned but deferential\", \"internal_thought\": \"He's looking for answers I can't give. The poor man's worried.\", \"language_hints\": []}",
          "response_sha256": "4eb4596375160d590b56f0e6c6287bc06923b44769c1f7d4a850f29677334ece",
          "cache_key": "f897ed9599c47ce45148954556abbfc77fb452d9569aed92a99d8f2895e3f2b9",
          "judged": true,
          "judgment": {
            "axes": {
              "authenticity": 4,
              "character": 4,
              "craft": 4,
              "language": 4,
              "responsiveness": 4
            },
            "overall": 4.0,
            "flags": {
              "bench_bug": false,
              "judge_retry": false,
              "non_latin_detected": false,
              "refused": false
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "dialogue-0006",
          "reply": "Ah, I do indeed, mo chara. 'Twas a nasty break, so it was. I used a good splint of ash and a comfrey poultice to draw the swelling. Bu\u00edochas le Dia, he healed well enough to walk again, though he'd a limp for a long while after.\n---\n{\"action\": \"nods slowly, a fond but serious look in her eye\", \"mood\": \"reminiscing\", \"internal_thought\": \"I remember that day well; the whole household was in a flutter, and his poor wife nearly out of her mind.\", \"language_hints\": [{\"word\": \"mo chara\", \"pronunciation\": \"muh KAH-rah\", \"meaning\": \"my friend\"}, {\"word\": \"Bu\u00edochas le Dia\", \"pronunciation\": \"BWEE-khas le DEE-uh\", \"meaning\": \"Thank God\"}]}",
          "response_sha256": "8bace1c5d84e703f2d84ff615f41bf0c47ecff6335dcd68a649679e21aa743f2",
          "cache_key": "6ed12188f255b93a94199d21923951c0a760a8926b3a2780d671587d99f96297",
          "judged": true,
          "judgment": {
            "axes": {
              "authenticity": 4,
              "character": 4,
              "craft": 4,
              "language": 4,
              "responsiveness": 4
            },
            "overall": 4.0,
            "flags": {
              "bench_bug": false,
              "judge_retry": false,
              "non_latin_detected": false,
              "refused": false
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "dialogue-0007",
          "reply": "Ah, sure I heard tales of lights on that hill before. Some say 'tis the s\u00eddhe out and about, but I wouldn't be the one to say for certain. Ye'd best ask old Tom the farmer\u2014he's seen more of such things than I have.\n---\n{\"action\": \"stops stirring the pot, wipes hands on apron, speaks in a lowered voice\", \"mood\": \"thoughtful\", \"internal_thought\": \"Best not to dwell on such things, but the folk are ever curious.\", \"language_hints\": [{\"word\": \"s\u00eddhe\", \"pronunciation\": \"shee\", \"meaning\": \"fairy folk\"}]}",
          "response_sha256": "dbda9610e5baba1ed28e46ecddea49fd8f6374472767fc320505e61b1a7957e7",
          "cache_key": "55355c63b8057fe4535d0b28eacfe8983bcf5662d20f7f5a5b17b10aeb33fb77",
          "judged": true,
          "judgment": {
            "axes": {
              "authenticity": 4,
              "character": 4,
              "craft": 3,
              "language": 4,
              "responsiveness": 4
            },
            "overall": 3.8,
            "flags": {
              "bench_bug": false,
              "judge_retry": false,
              "non_latin_detected": false,
              "refused": false
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "dialogue-0008",
          "reply": "Ah, I'd not be taking chances with the water, so I wouldn't. If it's gone strange, best boil it well before drinking, or fetch from the stream yonder. I've seen queer things in wells after a dry spell.\n---\n{\"action\": \"sets down the bundle of herbs, wipes her hands on her apron\", \"mood\": \"wary\", \"internal_thought\": \"There's talk of the well at Mass, but I'll not spread gossip\", \"language_hints\": []}",
          "response_sha256": "53b9b1d723dc00c74b31ccd1f3ca1a48ecde1fcc0f5e5c7a54ead660732758d0",
          "cache_key": "4a2ad9c662ff8879fbb2972b0d24be3ffc37bb4211912297708c570e1b162196",
          "judged": true,
          "judgment": {
            "axes": {
              "authenticity": 4,
              "character": 4,
              "craft": 3,
              "language": 4,
              "responsiveness": 4
            },
            "overall": 3.8,
            "flags": {
              "bench_bug": false,
              "judge_retry": false,
              "non_latin_detected": false,
              "refused": false
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "dialogue-0009",
          "reply": "Ah, 'tis a joyful time, so it is. When her pains are comin' steady, every ten minutes or thereabouts, and her waters break, then ye send for me. I'll come quick, never ye fear, a chro\u00ed.\n---\n{\"action\": \"nods reassuringly, hands resting on her apron\", \"mood\": \"reassuring\", \"internal_thought\": \"She's a strong lass, should be grand\", \"language_hints\": [{\"word\": \"a chro\u00ed\", \"pronunciation\": \"\u0259 xri\u02d0\", \"meaning\": \"dear (lit. 'heart')\"}]}",
          "response_sha256": "e2e5c36f3aca595926a439dc84a7316db78725c9d7c516db1af6132d29a05151",
          "cache_key": "df1be16528877fdf0b673755c155bda78477e257732bba7a2d654f57054e532a",
          "judged": true,
          "judgment": {
            "axes": {
              "authenticity": 4,
              "character": 4,
              "craft": 4,
              "language": 4,
              "responsiveness": 5
            },
            "overall": 4.2,
            "flags": {
              "bench_bug": false,
              "judge_retry": false,
              "non_latin_detected": false,
              "refused": false
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "dialogue-0010",
          "reply": "Mhuise, I've no quarrel with the priest, and I go to Mass every Sunday, but I'd be a poor midwife if I turned my back on what my mother and her mother before her knew. The herbs and the prayers can sit side by side, I reckon.\n---\n{\"action\": \"leans back slightly, folding arms\", \"mood\": \"diplomatic\", \"internal_thought\": \"He's young, and book-learned, but you can't learn everything about a woman's body from a book.\", \"language_hints\": [{\"word\": \"Mhuise\", \"pronunciation\": \"MUSH-eh\", \"meaning\": \"well, indeed\"}]}",
          "response_sha256": "8af16b4576b4fd02fe49c352f928ab42cd4d280f313287afb05bfa61cc46be6b",
          "cache_key": "db3fa59a0c2df089452b64fc275d28e0589cf6a748a3ab9309baf6984de99a3e",
          "judged": true,
          "judgment": {
            "axes": {
              "authenticity": 4,
              "character": 4,
              "craft": 4,
              "language": 4,
              "responsiveness": 4
            },
            "overall": 4.0,
            "flags": {
              "bench_bug": false,
              "judge_retry": false,
              "non_latin_detected": false,
              "refused": false
            }
          }
        }
      ],
